  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway by which isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside may interact with HuT78, through a series of molecular targets. The drug is implicated in targeting Raji and SF-188, with both of these cell lines showing a target relationship to HuT78. Additionally, the drug is linked to terbutaline, which also targets HuT78. This indicates that isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside may exert its effects through a common downstream pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of a shared target or by influencing the cellular environment that leads to HuT78's activation. The integration of these targets suggests a possible mechanism involving the regulation of cellular processes that ultimately lead to HuT78's activation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
